# Day 27 — Prior Authorization Story Simulator 🏥
> Part of my #60DaysOfClaudeAI challenge — building one AI-powered web app every day.
## What is this?
An interactive 8-scene story that walks you through the US healthcare Prior Authorization (PA) process — from patient diagnosis to insurance denial to final approval.
Follow **Rahul** (patient) and **Priya** (healthcare ops specialist) as they navigate one of the most confusing parts of the healthcare system — explained in beginner-friendly language.
## Scenes
| # | Scene | What Happens |
|---|-------|-------------|
| 1 | Doctor Visit | Rahul is diagnosed with RA. Dr. Patel prescribes Humira. |
| 2 | Insurance Roadblock | PA request submitted: Provider → Payer. No pharmacy involved. |
| 3 | What is PA? | Priya explains step therapy, treatment delays, AMA 2023 data. |
| 4 | Insurance Review | Eligibility, clinical docs, ICD-10 match, step therapy history. |
| 5 | Denial | PA denied — missing step therapy documentation. |
| 6 | Appeal | Letter of Medical Necessity + formal appeal filing. |
| 7 | Approval | PA approved, reference number issued, saved on file permanently. |
| 8 | Takeaways | Patient perspective + system metrics (denial rate, appeal rate, resolution time). |
## Tech Stack
- Single-file HTML
- Tailwind CSS (CDN)
- Vanilla JavaScript
- `createElement` + `appendChild` only — no `innerHTML` on chat container
## Key Concepts Covered
- Prior Authorization (PA) flow
- Step Therapy
- ICD-10 diagnosis codes
- Letter of Medical Necessity
- PA denial vs permanent denial
- Appeal process (standard 30 days / urgent 72 hours)
- System metrics: denial rate, appeal rate, resolution time
> StarCare Health is used as an illustrative payer example throughout — for educational purposes only.
## Run It
Just open `index.html` in any browser. No installs, no dependencies.
